1006 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A raga in Carnatic music is a melodic framework of specific notes designed to evoke distinct emotions and moods, often linked to therapeutic effects on the mind and body. The 10 recordings were carefully curated with specific ragas, each selected for its healing properties. Three songs featured Raga Sankarabharanam, known for promoting emotional balance and clarity. Two were based on Raga Madhyamavati, valued for its calming and stress-relieving qualities. Two utilized Raga Hamsadhwani, a cheerful and energizing raga. The remaining three songs were in Raga Maya-malava-gowla, often associated with enhancing focus and mindfulness. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1007 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Rehearsals for the songs were held for 2 hours, 3 times a week for 3 months leading up to Karunisai. To confirm musicians availabilities, we asked them to populate a spreadsheet with their availabilities throughout the week, from which we selected the times that most people could make. Once the rehearsal schedule was set, the other performers rearranged their commitments accordingly. Additionally, some of the artists who played the same part arranged to meet independently for sectional rehearsals for extra practice to ensure they were contributing their best to the ensemble.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
