1047 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Following the performances, the project team worked with the Temple of Music to ensure the seamless transfer of funds collected from ticket sales and additional donations. The $24,718 was wired directly to Chankanai Divisional Hospital in Sri Lanka and earmarked for the procurement of much-needed physiotherapy equipment. The funds facilitated the purchase of 150 stationary bicycles and 100 parallel bars, which were identified as critical tools for rehabilitation programs. Furthermore, the project included the delivery of 10 specially curated therapeutic Carnatic music recordings. These recordings were designed to complement physical therapy sessions, offering a holistic approach to healing and rehabilitation. The hospital administration estimated that these resources would benefit over 150 patients annually, significantly improving the quality of care provided at the facility.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1048 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (By December 20th, the hospital administration confirmed via email that the funds had been successfully received and allocated as intended. The Karunisai event not only achieved its financial goals but also left a lasting impact through its meaningful performances and the tangible benefits it brought to those in need.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
