1232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Initiating: We were successful in the initiating phase, but faced challenges managing multiple partnerships between Temple of Music, eSwara School, Renton IKEA Center, and Chankanai Hospital. The project operated more efficiently after focusing primarily on Temple of Music for musical direction and fund transfer, and eSwara School for our performers and donated resources. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
1233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Planning: The planning phase effectively balanced ambitious goals with realistic constraints - as shown by our detailed metrics, conservative $1,805 budget, and backup musician plans - but we learned that complex fund transfers between nonprofits require additional timeline buffers. We learned the lesson of building in extra time for inter-organizational processes from this project.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
1234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Monitoring and Controlling: We were successful in establishing checkpoints and reviewing our budget. We could do better in keeping track of During our controlling phase, we were successful in mitigating risks we encountered throughout the project and ensuring our team was on task.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
1235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Execution: Our execution demonstrated the value of leveraging existing partnerships - as shown by eSwara School's contribution of musicians and decorations which helped keep our budget under $2,500 - but revealed the need to expand marketing beyond our core South Asian audience to maximize the impact of our dual-performance structure at Renton IKEA Center.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
